# AmplifyUP — use the SDK, do not rebuild it

AmplifyUP SDK (`@amplifyup/sdk`) already owns layout resolve, Composer preview, Field/Slot/props context, personalization, page context, tracking, and the component-ID → render pipeline.

For placeable work, also follow the project skill `.cursor/skills/amplifyup-placeables/SKILL.md`.

## Hard rules

- **Do not reimplement SDK functionality** in this repository (no parallel “Amplify framework”).
- **Do not create** local catalogs, registries, ComponentRenderer wrappers, placeable indexes, or duplicate Edge/resolve/preview/pageContext helpers.
- **Do not expand** `renderAmplifyComponent` into a registry system. That file is only the thin `renderComponent` callback `AmplifyPageContent` requires: map `component_id` → existing React placeable, wrap with SDK `ComponentContextProvider`, return.
- **Trust projected props.** Use `useComponentProps()` and bind `value={live.fieldName}`. Do not merge `live` vs nested `post`, or build `resolve*`/`normalize*` layers to guess Edge shapes.
- **One field per SDK binding.** Never `landscapeImage || mainImage` (or similar) in `value={…}` — Composer maps to exactly one prop. Use `isComposerPreview()` only to change display, not to swap which field is bound.
- Before adding Amplify infrastructure, **read current SDK types/docs** (`@amplifyup/sdk/react`, `@amplifyup/sdk/server`). Prefer SDK exports over site-built equivalents.
- Site work for Amplify is: **placeable React components** (`Field` / `RichText` / `Image` / `Slot` / `useComponentProps` / `isComposerPreview`) and **page wiring** (`AmplifyPageContent`, `fetchPageConfigServer`, provider `pageContext`).
- **Do not fix Composer/product bugs in this site** (providers, polyfills, workarounds for Composer UI). Fix Composer/SDK or uptick the package.

## When adding a placeable

1. Create the React component; props interface matches Composer field names.
2. Register its `component_id` in AmplifyUP Composer (dashboard), not via a new site catalog.
3. Bind every editable field with SDK primitives and `value={live.…}` — no `name` + `value` together.
4. Add one entry to the existing `renderAmplifyComponent` map if the page uses that callback — nothing more.
5. Only null-check missing content when **not** in Composer (`!isComposerPreview()`).

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — local catalog / registry abstraction
const localCatalog = { Hero, ArticleGrid };
function ComponentRenderer({ componentId }) { ... }

// ❌ BAD — reimplementing resolve / preview / props context
fetch('/v1/resolve') // site-owned
const ComposerContext = createContext(...)

// ❌ BAD — fighting prop projection
const post = resolveAmplifyPost(field, props);
const img = live.landscapeImage || post.landscapeImage;

// ✅ GOOD — thin SDK renderComponent adapter only
const Component = map[componentId];
return (
  <ComponentContextProvider props={props} slots={slots} layoutNodeId={context?.layoutNodeId} componentId={componentId}>
    <Component {...props} />
  </ComponentContextProvider>
);

// ✅ GOOD — placeable uses SDK primitives and live props only
export function ArticleDetail() {
  const live = useComponentProps();
  return (
    <>
      <Image value={live.landscapeImage} />
      <h1><Field value={live.title} /></h1>
      <RichText value={live.body} />
    </>
  );
}
```
